<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following were the top 10 movies at the box office for the Friday-to-Sunday period, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc. Final numbers will be released on Monday.</p>
<p>    1 (*) Star Trek: First Contact .... $30.5 million</p>
<p>    2 (1) Space Jam ................... $16.6 million</p>
<p>    3 (2) Ransom ...................... $13.7 million</p>
<p>    4 (*) Jingle All the Way .......... $12.2 million</p>
<p>    5 (3) The Mirror Has Two Faces ....  $8.2 million</p>
<p>    6 (4) Set It Off ..................  $3.4 million</p>
<p>    7 (5) Romeo &amp; Juliet ..............  $3.2 million</p>
<p>    8(26) The English Patient .........  $2.7 million</p>
<p>    9 (6) Sleepers ..................... $1.4 million</p>
<p>   10 (7) The First Wives Club ......... $720,000</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Star Trek: First Contact&quot; and &quot;The First Wives Club&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.. &quot;Space Jam&quot; and &quot;Sleepers&quot; are released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc.. &quot;Ransom&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co.. &quot;Jingle All The Way&quot; and &quot;William Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet&quot; are released by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox. &quot;The Mirror Has Two Faces&quot; is released by Sony Corp.. &quot;Set It Off&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner. &quot;The English Patient&quot; is released by Disney's Miramax Films unit.</p>
